=== Text #9 ===
> Level 2 NVQ Diploma in Wood Occupations (Timber Frame Erection) - Q2W Ltd.
The Level 2 NVQ Diploma in Wood Occupations – Timber Frame Erection is designed to[ assess occupational] competence in the workplace.[ Lear]ners are required to demonstrate their skills, knowledge and[ experience] in the construction of timber frame buildings. This qualification is suitable for practicing timber frame carpenters.
This NVQ provides formal recognition[ of] practicing as timber frame carpenter.
There are no formal entry requirements for this NVQ qualification, however the potential[ lear]ner must be able to demonstrate[ that] they can meet the skills, knowledge and experience requirements of the NVQ in timber frame carpentry[ before enrolment].
The Level 2 NVQ Diploma in Wood Occupations – Timber Frame Erection qualifies the holder to apply for the Construction Skills Certification Scheme (CSCS) blue skill card (https://www.cscs.uk.com/card-type/manager/).

